This microscopic program allows you to add characters into the input
stream.  The only thing I use it for is a couple of places in my
bbstext.  Here are some examples:

---

(#249)  \n1\cfThat was the last scroll.\n1{#0PFiles:AddKeys Q`}

Automatically leaves the mail area when they've read the last one.

---

(#311)  \n1\b1\c9ASphincterSaysWhat!?!  \ce"\cb%s\ce"  Let's try the menu...
        \w1\n1{#0PFiles:AddKeys ?`}

When they enter a bad command, it automatically brings up a menu for them.

---

(#408)  \c0
(#409)  \c0{#0PFiles:AddKeys `}

Line #408 is the 'you may select other files at this time...' line and #409
is the 'describing your uploads now is OPTIONAL:' line.

I didn't like that because most files have diz files now anyway, so that
was a waste of time.  Soooo, I made that invisible by having no text,
changing the color to black so the end-of-input-dot wouldn't be seen and
finally adding a return to the input stream.

---

If you have any other interesting uses for it, please let me know...

The above {'s are actually control-Q commands, \'s are control-Y commands
and remember to modify the path to where you placed the "AddKeys" script.
